e villain deck counts to 25. So for any card that did multiple things, I simply picked a category for it according to an order of operations that I set, and then mentioned it in other sections. That&#39;s what the bracket means in the deck stats. Chrono-Ranger is a good example of this. Only 3 (5) of his cards do only single target dmg - two equpiment pieces and Terrible Tech-Strike. But he has [+7 (22)] cards that deal dmg and do other things - stuff like Bounty Board, Sudden Contract, or the Dart Thrower.&nbsp;</p><p>I think the rest of the stuff is self-explanatory. Any feedback would be greatly appreciated.&nbsp;</p>",
